.policy "waves-function-awaits" revision 1
.description "A function whose body awaits, at any depth: descendants of each def, as a closure over child edges."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"
// A closure of one level (decision 0095 §5, 0098 §1): a def's descendants, walked down the tree. Each def's subtree
// is a component of the reach graph, so its bit rows are pieces of their own.
.decl wf_tree(p: node, c: node)
wf_tree(p, c) :- child(p, c, _).
.decl wf_desc(f: node, n: node)
wf_desc(f, n) :- kind(f, "function_definition"), wf_tree(f, n).
wf_desc(f, m) :- wf_desc(f, n), wf_tree(n, m).
.violation WF1(at: node) code "WF1" "this function awaits somewhere in its body"
WF1(f) :- wf_desc(f, n), kind(n, "await").
